The chocolate cake is very sweet.
Now I am very thirsty.
The waiter walks past my table.
"Excuse me," I say politely.
He stops and comes to me.
"Yes, please?" the waiter asks.
"I would like a water," I say.
"Could I please have a bottle of mineral water?"
"Gladly."
"Sparkling or still?" he asks.
"Sparkling, please," I answer.
"Coming right up," the waiter says.
He goes briefly to the counter.
He is back quickly.
He brings the water and a glass.
He puts the bottle on my table.
"Here is your water, here you go," he says.
"Thank you very much," I answer.
I pour the cold water into my glass.
I take a big sip.
That is very refreshing.
